      "status": "expected-untested",
      "statement": "Handbook evidence record EV-MATH-0001 marks 6 of its counts for this function as CPU-scoped: the counted result depends on how the host CPU executes x87 instructions. Every reading recorded here was taken on an AMD Zen 2 processor or on a host whose CPU was not recorded; no reading on an Intel CPU, a Mac or Excel for the web exists, so a CPU difference is neither observed nor ruled out. OxFunc found Excel's last bit here follows the x87 F2XM1/FYL2X microcode on the hardest inputs (about 1 in 30). A dump of those x87 primitives on an AMD Zen 2 and an AMD Zen 1 host (Excel only on the first) differed on none of 3,157 rows (2026-08-23); Intel against AMD is untested.",
